Package: hifiberry-songcompare
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: interactive A/B comparison tool for versions of the same song
 SongCompare plays two or more renderings of the same recording and switches
 between them on a keypress, crossfading so the switch itself is inaudible.
 It is meant for listening tests: lossy against lossless, one master against
 another, a filter or EQ change against the unprocessed source.
 .
 Before playback it levels the files to a common RMS target and, on request,
 aligns them by cross-correlation, so that what is left to hear is the
 difference under test rather than a loudness or timing offset. An anonymous
 mode hides the filenames and shuffles the order until the comparison is over.
 .
 Reads MP3, AAC, ALAC, FLAC, WAV, OGG, M4A and MKV via Symphonia, and resamples
 when the output device does not support the source rate.
